--- OLD
 @BW: .BYTE $F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0
--- NEW
 @BW: .BYTE $F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0,$F0

;  Shop Information reaches these from the options chunk, where following the
;  pointers above would mean an indirect long read.  It indexes the tables
;  directly instead, as lut_MagicPermisPtr + 24 + class * 8 + level, which
;  holds only while they stay contiguous, eight bytes each and in class order.
.assert @FT - lut_MagicPermisPtr = 24, error, "magic permission pointer table changed size"
.assert @BW + 8 - @FT = 12 * 8, error, "magic permission tables are no longer contiguous"
